| 17                        | MTH 111 MTH 132 MTH 154 MTH 155 MTH 161 + MDE 61 |

#### GED-Math

| **If a student has. . .** | **The student may enroll in. . .** |
| ------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| 165 or above              | MTH 111 MTH 132 MTH 154 MTH 155    |
| 155-164 range             | MTH 111 MTH 132 MTH 154 + MDE 54   |
| 154 or below              | MDE 10                             |

\# Students may complete the VPT for placement.

English placement will be determined using one of the following measures.

## Table E: Student English Course Placement

| **If a student has…**                        | **The student may enroll in…**        |
| -------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| 6 or more years since high school graduation | Informed Self-Placement (see Advisor) |

### U.S.-based High School Grade Point Average (U.S.-based HS GPA) for English Placement

| **If a student has…**           | **The student may enroll in…** |
| ------------------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Less than 2.0 U.S.-based HS GPA | EDE 10                         |
| 2.0 to 2.99 U.S.-based HS GPA   | EDE 11 + ENG 111 ENG 115       |
| 3.0+ U.S.-based HS GPA          | ENG 111 ENG 115                |

| **Course**       | **Minimum Placement Requirement\*** |
| ---------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| EDE 10           | 1.99 or lower U.S.-based HS GPA     |
| EDE 11 + ENG 111 | 2.0 to 2.99 U.S.-based HS GPA       |
| ENG 111          | 3.0 or higher U.S.-based HS GPA     |
| ENG 115          | 2.0 or higher U.S.-based HS GPA     |

_\* U.S.-based High School Grade Point Average (HS GPA) is valid for six (6) years after the date of high school graduation. Students who completed U.S.-based high school more than six (6) years ago will be enrolled based on self-informed placement. Minimum Placement Requirement apply only to those who graduated high school six (6) years ago or less._

### SAT/ACT/GED Scores for English Placement

_(SAT, ACT and GED Test scores are valid for six (6) years after the date of the test.)_

### SAT-ERW Evidenced Based Reading & Writing

| **Student Score** | **The student may enroll in…** |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------ |
| 400-470           | EDE 11 + ENG 111               |
| 480 or above      | ENG 111                        |

### ACT Subject Area Tests: English & Reading

| **Student Score** | **The student may enroll in…** |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------ |
| 14 or below       | EDE 10                         |
| 15-17             | EDE 11 + ENG 111               |
| 18 or above       | ENG 111                        |

### GED English

| **Student Score** | **The student may enroll in…** |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------ |
| 165 or above      | ENG 111                        |

Any student who is not placed by the criteria listed above will be required to meet with an advisor in regards to Informed Placement and Direct Enrollment.

Official SAT or ACT scores should be submitted to the Admissions and Records office. An official report can be requested at [www.collegeboard.org](https://www.collegeboard.org/).

The counselors or English and mathematics faculty will document all mitigating circumstances that suggest an exception to the above placement rules.
